                      </capturedDeltas>
                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='Between the ages of 28-37, individuals with a credit score in the lowest range (300), a maximum loan tenure, and a marital status of single, have a 10.45% probability of defaulting. This trend is especially prominent for loans intended for business purposes among self-employed individuals.' captured-sheet='Defaults Vs Credit Score Analysis' id='4'>
                      <capturedDeltas>
