                    </story-point>
                    <story-point caption='In contrast, individuals aged 48-57, with a credit score ranging between 500-550, and a loan term of 37 months, primarily availed loans for education purposes. Despite having the highest interest rates, they showed the lowest default rates, especially among those employed part-time.' captured-sheet='Defaults Vs Credit Score Analysis' id='5'>
